eMaker JumpStart. Deploy it to a SageMaker AI endpoint in your own AWS account using SageMaker Studio or the SageMaker Python SDK, and run your first inference request.","primaryTopic":"open-source","topics":["open-source"],"sources":[{"name":"AWS Machine Learning Blog","url":"https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/machine-learning/metas-muse-spark-open-now-available-in-amazon-sagemaker-jumpstart/","type":"blog"}],"publishedAt":"2026-10-15T17:43:35Z","dateSource":"feed","discoveredAt":"2026-10-16T09:55:26Z","ingestedAt":"2026-10-17T09:28:31Z","isNew":true,"score":43.68,"importance":1,"related":["s-9b317f01752a","s-ba8a6ffbbe0f","s-1241afcd37b6","s-eb89e877408d","s-1ccfdcacfd19","s-f5b98f32f035"],"cluster":"open-source","x":786.3,"y":691.6},{"id":"s-01bfc0baca35","title":"DPA-MoE: A Runtime Precision Control Framework for MoE Inference","kind":"paper","summary":"Mixture-of-Experts (MoE) models reduce computation by routing each token to a small set of experts, but each selected expert is still used at a fixed precision. We present DPA-MoE, a runtime precision control framework that makes routed experts any-precision.","whyItMatters":"arXiv paper, first version published Oct 16, 2026.","primaryTopic":"research","topics":["research"],"sources":[{"name":"arXiv","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.21378","type":"arxiv"}],"publishedAt":"2026-10-16T04:00:00Z","dateSource":"arxiv-v1","discoveredAt":"2026-10-16T09:55:26Z","ingestedAt":"2026-10-16T09:55:26Z","isNew":true,"score":43.34,"importance":1,"related":["s-7812c6f721af","s-4011f2924678","s-077dd035a4f1","s-12dc0bb24a10","s-1213af61c8a4","s-1b3c34ee9442"],"cluster":"research","x":1333.0,"y":484.4},{"id":"s-046a4991ca05","title":"When Models Misread Ink: Auditing VLMs for Arabic Calligraphy Recognition","kind":"paper","summary":"Arabic calligraphy is a high-stakes cultural visual domain for Muslim communities, yet VLM evaluations rarely test its fine-grained script traditions. We audit 12 VLMs on a cleaned 1,195-image six-way benchmark using numeric, visual-cue, and Diwani-first prompts.","whyItMatters":"arXiv paper, first version published Oct 16, 2026.","primaryTopic":"multimodal","topics":["multimodal","research"],"sources":[{"name":"arXiv","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.22018","type":"arxiv"}],"publishedAt":"2026-10-16T04:00:00Z","dateSource":"arxiv-v1","discoveredAt":"2026-10-16T09:55:26Z","ingestedAt":"2026-10-16T09:55:26Z","isNew":true,"score":43.34,"importance":1,"related":["s-07977627d9db","s-17af6167f10c","s-e812566e88ff","s-b382a6d08a5f","s-083281616cd8","s-11e293f4bf59"],"cluster":"multimodal","x":1189.2,"y":455.1},{"id":"s-0610369902be","title":"PRISM: PRIvileged Sibling-guided Multi-Agent Topology Design","kind":"paper","summary":"Multi-agent systems (MAS) based on large language models (LLMs) have become a powerful way to address complex problems, and their effectiveness depends critically on the collaboration topology that decides which agents participate and how they communicate.","whyItMatters":"arXiv paper, first version published Oct 16, 2026.","primaryTopic":"llms","topics":["llms","agents","research"],"sources":[{"name":"arXiv","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.20628","type":"arxiv"}],"publishedAt":"2026-10-16T04:00:00Z","dateSource":"arxiv-v1","discoveredAt":"2026-10-16T09:55:26Z","ingestedAt":"2026-10-16T09:55:26Z","isNew":true,"score":43.34,"importance":1,"related":["s-12dd638496e8","s-0a271f839c02","s-0cbbb4ebf20a","s-0e1a49b23617","s-0e83cd4444ce","s-140323b58460"],"cluster":"llms","x":639.1,"y":285.7},{"id":"s-06a30eacc1d6","title":"ReState: Noise-Level-Aware State Correction for Training-Free Object Removal in Few-Step Diffusion Models","kind":"paper","summary":"Training-free object removal commonly redirects self-attention away from the target region, but on few-step distilled diffusion models this often leaves object-shaped residuals.","whyItMatters":"arXiv paper, first version published Oct 16, 2026.","primaryTopic":"generative","topics":["generative","research"],"sources":[{"name":"arXiv","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.21287","type":"arxiv"}],"publishedAt":"2026-10-16T04:00:00Z","dateSource":"arxiv-v1","discoveredAt":"2026-10-16T09:55:26Z","ingestedAt":"2026-10-16T09:55:26Z","isNew":true,"score":43.34,"importance":1,"related":["s-001bb0d836c0","s-0740059b32b7","s-15306626eabf","s-f930bda97616","s-65442e708214"],"cluster":"generative","x":1508.4,"y":741.0},{"id":"s-0740059b32b7","title":"UltraDiff: Transferring High-Fidelity Priors to Compressed Latent Spaces for High-Resolution Image Generation","kind":"paper","summary":"High-resolution synthesis with Latent Diffusion Models (LDMs) faces a fundamental trade-off between computational cost and generative fidelity. This trade off is largely governed by the latent compression factor f (e.g. f8 denotes f=8 and f32 f=32).","whyItMatters":"arXiv paper, first version published Oct 16, 2026.","primaryTopic":"generative","topics":["generative","research"],"sources":[{"name":"arXiv","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.21202","type":"arxiv"}],"publishedAt":"2026-10-16T04:00:00Z","dateSource":"arxiv-v1","discoveredAt":"2026-10-16T09:55:26Z","ingestedAt":"2026-10-16T09:55:26Z","isNew":true,"score":43.34,"importance":1,"related":["s-001bb0d836c0","s-06a30eacc1d6","s-15306626eabf","s-f930bda97616","s-65442e708214"],"cluster":"generative","x":1450.9,"y":747.2},{"id":"s-077dd035a4f1","title":"Task-Phase-Conditioned Expert Routing Is Not a Reliable Proxy for Quantization Sensitivity in MoE FFN Tensors","kind":"paper","summary":"We investigate whether per-layer, per-task-phase (prompt/reasoning/response) expert-routing statistics in a Mixture-of-Experts (MoE) language model can guide layer-wise mixed-precision quantization of routed-expert FFN tensors (down/gate and up).","whyItMatters":"arXiv paper, first version published Oct 16, 2026.","primaryTopic":"infra","topics":["infra","research"],"sources":[{"name":"arXiv","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.20826","type":"arxiv"}],"publishedAt"